# PushBox — Project TODO

## Bug Fixes

### Critical

- [ ] **Purchase popover appears off-centre on visionOS.**
  The store sheet anchor is displaced left or right instead of appearing directly in front
  of the user. Investigate the popover attachment point in `GameToolbarOrnament` and
  `SolutionCreditsStoreView`.

- [ ] **Level Selector sheet lingers when tapping Next / Previous.**
  The sheet should close immediately when the user navigates to the next or previous level.
  Audit the `onChange` handler in `GameChangeHandlers` and ensure `isLevelSheetPresented`
  is set to `false` before the level transition begins.

## Gameplay

- [ ] **Implement tap-to-move on the puzzle grid.** Learn from lego game and watch again their video, install and pay for their game
  Allow the player to tap an empty floor tile to automatically pathfind and walk there.
  Keep the D-Pad and swipe gestures as fallback input methods. Consider leveraging the
  existing `GridPosition` model for pathfinding.

- [ ] **Ensure the level is in a clean state before running a solution.**
  If the player has made moves, the level should be reset to its initial state before
  solution playback begins. Options: auto-reset silently, or present a confirmation
  ("Reset and show solution?"). Add this step to `startSolution()` in the game view.

- [ ] **Volume placement: add lock / unlock position toggle (visionOS).**
  Placement logic already exists in `ImmersiveGameView+Placement.swift`. Add a
  Lock / Unlock button to the ornament so users can reposition the board after initial
  placement (reference: JigSpace behaviour).

## Platform

### macOS

- [ ] **Fix app lifecycle on quit.**: Maybe that was already fixed for VisionOS at least. 
  When the user closes the macOS window the game should fully terminate. Verify window-
  close and right-click menu behaviour against the macOS HIG. Cross-check the reasons
  from the previous App Store rejection and confirm each is resolved before resubmitting.

### App Store

  Should I add tvOS? does it worth it? challenging?

## Input

- [ ] **Hand gesture input for visionOS.**
  Investigate spatial tap and pinch-to-select gestures via ARKit / RealityKit to allow
  the user to move the player by tapping a target tile or swiping in the immersive space in direction of movement or using controllers
  without using the D-Pad.

## Localization

- [ ] **Translate the app into additional languages.**
  Audit all user-visible strings in SwiftUI views and `AppIntents` for `String(localized:)`
  or `LocalizedStringResource` usage. Add `Localizable.xcstrings` and submit translations
  for at minimum: French, German, Spanish, Japanese, and Simplified Chinese.

